# Keep the scripts, the Compose files and the nginx config directory tracked
# even where a user-level excludes file ignores those names.
!*.sh
!docker-compose.yaml
!**/nginx/
!**/nginx/**

# Shared non-secret configuration is config/env/common.env, not a dotfile,
# because a user-level `.env` rule is common.
#
# Verify after adding anything new, because the failure is silent:
#   git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard
#
# That should list `secrets/`, `.tmp/`, `.state/`, the cached ingress manifest,
# any generated cluster overlay, and one env file per site created here --
# and nothing else. Anything unexpected in it is a build input that has gone
# invisible, which is the failure the negations above exist to prevent.

# Actually ignore: generated, downloaded or machine-local state.
.tmp/
.state/
cluster/ingress-nginx.yaml
secrets/
*.local.yaml

# A SITE IS MACHINE STATE, NOT A DECLARATION THIS REPOSITORY MAKES. Creating a
# store with `make new-site` writes one of these and destroying it removes one,
# so tracking them turns "I needed a scratch store for an afternoon" into two
# commits about a store nobody else has. Which stores exist here is a fact
# about this laptop, and `make sites` reads the filesystem to answer it.
#
# The file is not lost by being untracked: it is DERIVED from the hostname by
# scripts/site.sh, and `make new-site` writes an equivalent one. What is not
# recoverable is the store's data, which was never in git either.
k8s/base/config/env/sites/*.env

# EXCEPT the default site, and this is not sentiment about the first store --
# k8s/base/kustomization.yaml names this exact path in its configMapGenerator.
# Without it a fresh clone cannot render either overlay, so `make lint` fails
# on a checkout that has done nothing wrong. It is also the worked example the
# generated ones are read against.
!k8s/base/config/env/sites/vanilla-test.env
# Generated by scripts/deploy.sh when the cluster is pointed at a site other
# than the base's own. Machine state: it names whichever store this cluster is
# serving today.
k8s/overlays/site/
# and the throwaway a dry run builds beside it
k8s/overlays/.site-*/

# TLS for SITE_HOST, read at bootstrap and never committed. Point CERTS_HOME
# somewhere else, or put <host>.crt and <host>.key here.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. `certs/` matches a directory
# and a symlink is not one, so pointing this at a shared mkcert directory --
# the obvious thing to do -- left the link itself committable while every file
# under it looked ignored. `git check-ignore certs/anything` cannot even be
# asked once the link exists: it refuses with "beyond a symbolic link".
certs

# Disposable output: build products, screenshots, working images, scratch
# notes. Nothing here is reviewed and nothing here is committed.
#
# It carries its own line because the machine this was written on hides it
# through a user-level excludes file, and a clone has none of that.
local.d/
